					<p class="body1" align="left"><span class="body1 style73"> <h2>News archive</h2><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-02-07 | Wednesday</font></strong><br><br>happy <strong>J-Dilla&#39;s Born Day</strong> folkers.<br /><br />and how appropriate that today is the birthday of one of the illest producers of all time... it&#39;s that <strong>Tall Homie Vitamin D&#39;s Big Tune Beat Battle</strong> this evening at War Room.  i&#39;ll be there, so will will a number of the towns filthiest beatmakers.<br /><br />in bigger news, our boy <strong>Gabriel Teodros</strong> and his single <strong>&quot;No Label&quot;</strong> is the <strong>#1 Most Added</strong> to rotation this week at <strong>CMJ Hip Hop</strong>.  he&#39;s also got a review coming up in <strong>Rolling Stone</strong>.  goodness gracious, that is big news!  if you see the everyday journeyman walking the South Seattle beat, give him a big up and congrats.<br /><br />the <strong>Blue Scholars BAYANI Album Release Party</strong> is confirmed for <strong>May 11/12</strong>.  tickets are on sale now for two back to back shows at <strong>The Showbox</strong> for your scholarly pleasure.  the line up will include <strong>Big World Breaks</strong> + a four-piece horn section as our band, as well as a reunion of Seattle/Tacoma veterans <strong>Black Anger</strong> with the Pacific Northwest.  goodness gracious me (no, not the discontinued South Asian sketch comedy show on BBC, the explicative!) that&#39;s BIG NEWS.  email me if you caught that reference.<br /><br />you can get presale tix <a href="http://www.ticketmaster.com/artist/1103485/?search_redirect=blue%20scholars&amp;tm_link=tm_header_search">here</a>.&nbsp; (the password is &quot;massline&quot;)<br /><br />also, it looks like a dispute has halted <strong>Lt. Watada&#39;s court-martial</strong>.  read more about it <a href="http://www.thankyoult.org/content/view/1015/29/">here</a>.<br /><br />til next time, catch me at 20th and Jackson with the folkers.<br /><br />injera and mitmita powder is what&#39;s on my mind.<br /><br />saba

<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-02-05 | Monday</font></strong><br><br>peace y&#39;all.<br /><br />another football season has passed with the exciting conclusion of the super bowl (who watches the pro bowl anyway). this year, the fumbles made by the corporate sponsors were bigger than those on the field. companies who paid millions of dollars for super bowl spots gave us the opportunity this year to laugh at <a href="http://youtube.com/watch?v=hw_kHH3zJGY"><strong>immigrants</strong></a> as well as reminding us that it&#39;s funny and ok to be <a href="http://youtube.com/watch?v=TcwBvM8XUIg"><strong>homophobic</strong></a>. im not sure what other &#39;interesting&#39; commercials were shown because i left the house after watching <a href="http://youtube.com/watch?v=H97y459pOis"><strong>prince&#39;s halftime show</strong></a> (i only tuned in to see this anyway), which might be the GOAT superbowl performance. i wonder if there have been any complaints about how phallic prince&#39;s guitar looked when they projected his silhouette onto that large sheet. just an observation ;)<br /><br />peace<br />dj daps1<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-02-02 | Friday</font></strong><br><br>Wrote a good long post and right as I submitted it, everything got lost. Here&#39;s a rough outline of what was once a meticulously crafted post.<br /><br />1. DVS Crew&#39;s Sneke (who did Blue Scholars handstyle) featured in January&#39;s Mass Appeal magazine. <br /><br />2. Abyssinian Creole, Canary Sing, good peoples and good eats tonight at Hidmo!<br /><br />3. Happy Birthday to the folkers: Khalil, my biggest little sister Mo, Big Sexy Jojo, That Dude daps1, OG manager Bobby. 30 is the new 20!<br /><br />4. Saturday, Feb. 3: Massive Monkees and Big World Breaks present 4 the Love: A Tribute to James Brown at the Nectar in Fremont.<br /><br />Be easy.<br /><br />geo<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-02-01 | Thursday</font></strong><br><br>Your comrade Geo here again, taking a break between episodes of <strong>The Wire</strong> (thanks to Arjay for the DVD sets!).<br /><br />This weekend I reclaim my inner primate and cheer on other grown men in uniform. I&#39;ll be pulling for the <strong>Chicago Bears</strong> (same reason I always
pulled for the cat who beat me in a battle). While the ultra-militant
homies shake their heads at my indulgence in the Greatest American
Distraction of All Time, you can find me on Friday (2/2) discussing the
<strong>Super Bowl</strong> with the <strong>Gasman</strong> himself on<strong> KJR-950AM</strong> (Seattle) at <strong>5pm</strong>.<br /><br />Later that evening, the good folks at <strong>Resident Media</strong> and <strong>Rags to Riches</strong> will be throwing a party featuring an all-star lineup of DJs: <strong>Babu of Dilated Peoples</strong>, <strong>Kuttin Kandi</strong>, and<br /><strong>D-Double</strong>. It goes down at <strong>The War Room</strong> on <strong>Friday, February 2</strong>. Now that right there is the illest lineup of Filipino DJs since been pimpin. All for 5 bucks. <br /><br />Back to <em>The Wire</em>...<br /><br /><br /><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-01-31 | Wednesday</font></strong><br><br>Thirty-one days into 2007 and still no sign of a dope hip-hop album (am I sleeping? let me know...). With the <em>White Rapper Show</em> being 2007&#39;s lone highlight so far, that&#39;s not a good look. Maybe <strong>Nas</strong> was right. If the drought doesn&#39;t end by mid-February, at least we got my man <strong>GT</strong>&#39;s<strong><em> Lovework</em></strong> album to look forward to. That and <strong>J-Dilla&#39;s <em>Jay Love Japan</em></strong> import.<br /><br />Peace to <strong>Hari Kondabolu</strong>
(who killed it at the Massline comedy show last Friday). Aside from
being politically sharp, hilarious and handsome, dude is getting some
shine in the media. Check the article on <a href="http://http://seattlepi.nwsource.com/ae/301391_comedy29.html">Hari and the local progressive comic scene in the Seattle Post-Intelligencer</a>.<br /><br /><div align="left">Tacoma got love for Massline and <strong>Lt. Watada</strong>, and it was evident last Saturday at Hell&#39;s Kitchen with cameras rolling<br />for
MTV, NHK and Al-Jazeera. Like homie said onstage, he&#39;ll probably be
going to jail for a long time for speaking up, so the least we can do
is show some support. On February 5, you can catch me at Fort Lewis on
the day of Lietenant Ehren Watada&#39;s court-martial. For More info, hit
up <a href="http://www.thankyoult.org">www.thankyoult.org.</a><br /><br /></div>The place to be tonight in the 206 is the University of Washington HUB Ballroom, where <strong>Lupe Fiasco</strong> headlines an all-star 206 line-up featuring Massline reps <strong>Common Market</strong> and <strong>Gabriel Teodros</strong> along with <strong>Massive Monkees</strong>,<strong> Choklate</strong> and <strong>Dyme Def</strong>.<br />
<br />
Peace,<br />
geo<br /><br /><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><center><div class="pagenumbers"><A HREF="archive.php?from=220">[&lt;&lt;]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=0">[1]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=5">[2]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=10">[3]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=15">[4]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=20">[5]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=25">[6]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=30">[7]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=35">[8]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=40">[9]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=45">[10]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=50">[11]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=55">[12]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=60">[13]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=65">[14]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=70">[15]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=75">[16]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=80">[17]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=85">[18]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=90">[19]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=95">[20]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=100">[21]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=105">[22]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=110">[23]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=115">[24]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=120">[25]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=125">[26]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=130">[27]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=135">[28]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=140">[29]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=145">[30]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=150">[31]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=155">[32]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=160">[33]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=165">[34]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=170">[35]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=175">[36]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=180">[37]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=185">[38]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=190">[39]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=195">[40]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=200">[41]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=205">[42]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=210">[43]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=215">[44]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=220">[45]</A> [46] <A HREF="archive.php?from=230">[47]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=235